<section class="wrap reveal" id="project-abstract" aria-labelledby="project-abstract-title">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated project-abstract">
    <div class="project-abstract-copy">
      <p class="kicker">Project abstract</p>
      <h2 id="project-abstract-title">Geometry, Integration and the Conditions of Return</h2>
      <p class="lede">The Two Infinities is an independent theoretical research project investigating whether
        asymptotic limits, complex rotation, integration and orientation-reversing topology can be organised
        into one speculative model of existence, conscious continuity, gravitational mass, temporal direction
        and cosmic recurrence.</p>

      <p>The inquiry proceeds in four stages. It first separates established mathematical and physical results
        from the meanings assigned to them; it then states each interpretive promotion as a bridge hypothesis;
        it identifies the dimensions, fields, conservation laws and covariant equations a physical mechanism
        would require; and it compares any proposed consequence with conventional explanations and declared
        failure conditions. In this structure, \(\pi\) supplies closure, \(i\) supplies complex phase, integration
        supplies bounded history, and toroidal or M&ouml;bius geometry supplies candidate forms of return. These
        relations define the programme&rsquo;s dependency chain, not a proof that one domain entails the next.</p>

      <p>The present result is therefore a research architecture rather than a completed cosmology. Its principal
        open problems are to derive a lawful coupling between accumulated differentials and stress&ndash;energy, name
        a carrier for any residue that survives inversion, calibrate the Cosmic Ledger independently, and produce
        observations that distinguish the framework from ordinary astrophysics. The Zero-Seam protocol provides
        the current empirical edge: competing models are specified in advance so that the proposed integration
        signal may be retained, revised or rejected by the data.</p>

      <p class="formula">\[
        \text{result}\;\longrightarrow\;\text{bridge hypothesis}\;\longrightarrow\;
        \text{physical model}\;\longrightarrow\;\text{discriminating test}
      \]</p>
    </div>

